From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: utsure CI <utsure@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 3 May 2026 00:00:00 +0630
Subject: [PATCH] render: preserve RGBA allocation base when shift clipping

`shift_event()` can clip an RGBA image after collision resolution by moving
the visible top row to y=0. Advancing `ASS_ImageRGBA::rgba` loses the
allocation base, but the public `ass_free_images_rgba()` API later frees that
same field. Keep the base pointer stable and move the visible rows down inside
the existing allocation instead.
---
 libass/ass_render.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libass/ass_render.c b/libass/ass_render.c
index 68ba69419..c1ea732fd 100644
--- a/libass/ass_render.c
+++ b/libass/ass_render.c
@@ -5050,7 +5050,9 @@ shift_event(ASS_Renderer *render_priv, EventImages *ei, int shift)
         if (rcur->dst_y < 0) {
             int clip = -rcur->dst_y;
             rcur->h -= clip;
-            rcur->rgba += clip * rcur->stride;
+            if (rcur->h > 0)
+                memmove(rcur->rgba, rcur->rgba + clip * rcur->stride,
+                        (size_t) rcur->stride * rcur->h);
             rcur->dst_y = 0;
         }
         if (rcur->dst_y + rcur->h >= render_priv->height) {
